example-1: h = 1024, 2048 tokens per micro-batch, N = 4 GPUs, 2 bytes per value
  MLP weights: 8388608 values = 16.00 MiB; per GPU with tensor parallelism: 4.00 MiB
  forward work per GPU: 8.59e+09 floating-point operations (1/N of 3.44e+10)
  tensor parallelism: 1 all-reduce of 4.00 MiB in forward + 1 in backward per micro-batch; each GPU sends 12.00 MiB per micro-batch, on the critical path
  data parallelism instead: 1 all-reduce of the MLP gradient, 16.00 MiB, per step; each GPU sends 24.00 MiB per step, can overlap with backward

example-1-N8: h = 1024, 2048 tokens per micro-batch, N = 8 GPUs, 2 bytes per value
  MLP weights: 8388608 values = 16.00 MiB; per GPU with tensor parallelism: 2.00 MiB
  forward work per GPU: 4.29e+09 floating-point operations (1/N of 3.44e+10)
  tensor parallelism: 1 all-reduce of 4.00 MiB in forward + 1 in backward per micro-batch; each GPU sends 14.00 MiB per micro-batch, on the critical path
  data parallelism instead: 1 all-reduce of the MLP gradient, 16.00 MiB, per step; each GPU sends 28.00 MiB per step, can overlap with backward

example-2-short: h = 4096, 512 tokens per micro-batch, N = 8 GPUs, 2 bytes per value
  MLP weights: 134217728 values = 256.00 MiB; per GPU with tensor parallelism: 32.00 MiB
  forward work per GPU: 1.72e+10 floating-point operations (1/N of 1.37e+11)
  tensor parallelism: 1 all-reduce of 4.00 MiB in forward + 1 in backward per micro-batch; each GPU sends 14.00 MiB per micro-batch, on the critical path
  data parallelism instead: 1 all-reduce of the MLP gradient, 256.00 MiB, per step; each GPU sends 448.00 MiB per step, can overlap with backward

